1
00:00:03,666 --> 00:00:05,500
Stung by Dear Uncle’s insult, Agha Jan

2
00:00:05,541 --> 00:00:06,875
Was so angry,

3
00:00:06,875 --> 00:00:09,000
That he was always looking for a chance to get even.

4
00:00:09,625 --> 00:00:11,250
The night that Dear Uncle Napoleon,

5
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:12,541
Afraid of a thief,

6
00:00:12,625 --> 00:00:14,250
Hid under the bed…

7
00:00:14,250 --> 00:00:16,375
Agha Jan got his chance.

8
00:00:16,750 --> 00:00:17,750
He decided

9
00:00:17,750 --> 00:00:19,625
To give a lavish party,

10
00:00:19,625 --> 00:00:22,166
And by inviting the thief to the party,

11
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:25,041
To mock Dear Uncle’s boasting.

12
00:00:25,625 --> 00:00:28,125
Dear Uncle, seeing his reputation at risk,

13
00:00:28,125 --> 00:00:30,041
In another corner of the garden,

14
00:00:30,125 --> 00:00:31,875
Held a mourning ceremony,

15
00:00:31,875 --> 00:00:33,250
And the party fell apart.

16
00:00:34,375 --> 00:00:35,916
Agha Jan, as planned,

17
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:37,375
Showed up uninvited at the ceremony,

18
00:00:37,375 --> 00:00:38,125
But Dear Uncle,

19
00:00:38,125 --> 00:00:39,875
Who had seen through his plan,

20
00:00:39,916 --> 00:00:41,416
Once again, harshly,

21
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:43,125
Put Agha Jan firmly in his place.

22
00:00:44,291 --> 00:00:47,166
(Sound of horses galloping)

23
00:00:52,791 --> 00:00:54,916
Dear Uncle Napoleon Episode 3

24
00:00:56,041 --> 00:01:01,000
Based on the novel Dear Uncle Napoleon Written by Iraj Pezeshkzad

25
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:03,375
Subtitle : Iman Soleimani Zadeh

26
00:01:03,375 --> 00:01:05,375
(Sound of horses galloping)

27
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:08,750
(Sound of gunfire and warriors shouting)

28
00:02:07,875 --> 00:02:11,625
♪ Ride of the valkyrie ♪

29
00:02:58,875 --> 00:02:59,500
Thank you.

30
00:02:59,833 --> 00:03:00,833
Thank you very much.

31
00:03:01,250 --> 00:03:01,750
Ghasem

32
00:03:01,833 --> 00:03:02,458
Yes!

33
00:03:02,833 --> 00:03:05,125
That lamp is going out too.

34
00:03:05,333 --> 00:03:05,958
Yes, sir.

35
00:03:11,708 --> 00:03:12,791
By the way, sister!

36
00:03:12,916 --> 00:03:15,166
Why didn’t Dustali come to the ceremony tonight?!

37
00:03:15,666 --> 00:03:16,833
How do I know!

38
00:03:17,291 --> 00:03:18,291
Yes, why didn’t they?!

39
00:03:18,291 --> 00:03:19,916
Lady Aziz-Saltaneh didn’t come to the ceremony either!

40
00:03:19,958 --> 00:03:21,083
They must have gone somewhere else.

41
00:03:21,083 --> 00:03:22,541
I hope nothing’s wrong.

42
00:03:22,791 --> 00:03:24,416
Help me!

43
00:03:24,916 --> 00:03:26,666
Save me!

44
00:03:26,666 --> 00:03:28,291
It sounds like Dustali-Khan’s voice! - Ladder!

45
00:03:28,541 --> 00:03:29,958
It’s him! - Ladder!

46
00:03:29,958 --> 00:03:31,208
Mr. Dustali-Khan! - Hurry!

47
00:03:31,291 --> 00:03:31,958
- Ladder!

48
00:03:32,041 --> 00:03:33,541
Mr. Dustali-Khan, we’re coming.

49
00:03:33,583 --> 00:03:34,458
- Hurry…

50
00:03:34,458 --> 00:03:35,583
We’re coming! Don’t be afraid!

51
00:03:35,583 --> 00:03:36,166
What happened!

52
00:03:36,208 --> 00:03:38,541
By the late Great Sir’s soul, help me!

53
00:03:38,583 --> 00:03:39,708
Ghasem, ladder!

54
00:03:39,791 --> 00:03:40,791
Yes… yes! - Help!

55
00:03:40,791 --> 00:03:42,416
Bring the ladder, quick! - Help!

56
00:03:42,416 --> 00:03:43,791
- Ladder, quick!

57
00:03:43,791 --> 00:03:44,541
Move, Ghasem!

58
00:03:44,541 --> 00:03:45,291
Ladder!

59
00:03:45,333 --> 00:03:45,916
What happened?

60
00:03:45,916 --> 00:03:47,541
What is it, Dustali? - Come here, son!

61
00:03:47,541 --> 00:03:48,791
Mr. Dustali-Khan!

62
00:03:48,791 --> 00:03:49,583
What happened!

63
00:03:49,583 --> 00:03:50,708
Give me your hand!

64
00:03:50,791 --> 00:03:52,041
- I can’t, Sir! - What happened?

65
00:03:52,041 --> 00:03:52,958
Dustali,

66
00:03:52,958 --> 00:03:56,166
Why are you coming from the roof?

67
00:03:56,166 --> 00:03:57,083
Easy, easy!

68
00:03:57,166 --> 00:03:58,416
Careful with him, now.

69
00:03:58,416 --> 00:03:59,291
Give me your hand. - Hold him!

70
00:03:59,291 --> 00:04:00,333
Give me your hand, Dustali.

71
00:04:00,416 --> 00:04:01,208
Easy, now.

72
00:04:01,291 --> 00:04:02,083
Easy - Let…

73
00:04:02,166 --> 00:04:02,958
Easy - Let me get down.

74
00:04:03,041 --> 00:04:03,791
- What happened? - Easy

75
00:04:03,833 --> 00:04:05,791
(He groans)

76
00:04:05,833 --> 00:04:06,666
Oh, my God!

77
00:04:06,666 --> 00:04:07,333
Naked!

78
00:04:07,416 --> 00:04:08,291
Oh! Why!

79
00:04:08,333 --> 00:04:09,541
Dustali… Dustali!

80
00:04:09,541 --> 00:04:10,291
- Woe is me!

81
00:04:10,291 --> 00:04:10,916
Dustali!

82
00:04:10,958 --> 00:04:12,291
Woe is me!

83
00:04:12,291 --> 00:04:13,791
Why is he up on the roof naked?

84
00:04:13,791 --> 00:04:14,708
What’s wrong with him?

85
00:04:14,791 --> 00:04:15,416
Sir!

86
00:04:15,416 --> 00:04:17,166
Looks like a snake bit him!

87
00:04:17,166 --> 00:04:18,791
Talking nonsense again, Ghasem?

88
00:04:18,958 --> 00:04:20,916
Will you let me see what happened? - Clear the way.

89
00:04:21,208 --> 00:04:21,916
Dustali!

90
00:04:21,958 --> 00:04:22,583
What is it?

91
00:04:23,541 --> 00:04:24,125
Water!

92
00:04:24,125 --> 00:04:25,500
Splash water on his face!

93
00:04:26,125 --> 00:04:28,166
I stirred gold in his water to cure his fright!

94
00:04:28,750 --> 00:04:29,625
Cut! - Dustali!

95
00:04:29,625 --> 00:04:30,250
Cut!

96
00:04:30,250 --> 00:04:30,875
Dustali!

97
00:04:30,875 --> 00:04:31,541
Cut! - Cut what?

98
00:04:32,083 --> 00:04:32,666
Cut!

99
00:04:32,708 --> 00:04:33,416
Who wanted to cut?- - Who cut?

100
00:04:33,458 --> 00:04:34,541
She wanted to cut it off!

101
00:04:34,875 --> 00:04:36,000
Who wanted to cut?

102
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:36,750
- Good heavens! Who? - Aziz...

103
00:04:36,750 --> 00:04:37,791
- Aziz...

104
00:04:37,875 --> 00:04:38,750
What happened, Poori?

105
00:04:38,750 --> 00:04:41,000
Poor Dustali-Khan fainted.

106
00:04:41,125 --> 00:04:41,583
Dustali!

107
00:04:42,375 --> 00:04:42,750
What is it?

108
00:04:42,750 --> 00:04:43,375
Dustali!

109
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:45,541
Cut!... cut!

110
00:04:45,541 --> 00:04:47,250
Well, cut what? - She wanted to cut it off!

111
00:04:47,250 --> 00:04:48,750
She wanted to cut it off! Cut off what?!

112
00:04:48,750 --> 00:04:49,500
Aziz!

113
00:04:49,916 --> 00:04:50,500
Aziz!

114
00:04:50,916 --> 00:04:52,416
What on earth did she want to cut?!

115
00:04:52,416 --> 00:04:53,625
That she-demon…

116
00:04:53,666 --> 00:04:55,666
Cut off what?

117
00:04:57,083 --> 00:04:57,833
Moment!

118
00:04:57,833 --> 00:04:59,208
Moment!

119
00:04:59,250 --> 00:05:00,708
Let me see! Let me see!

120
00:05:00,708 --> 00:05:02,583
Lady Aziz-Saltaneh wanted to, God forbid…

121
00:05:02,583 --> 00:05:05,250
Yes! (He speaks with horror)

122
00:05:05,250 --> 00:05:06,500
She wanted to cut it off!

123
00:05:06,500 --> 00:05:07,708
She wanted to cut it off!

124
00:05:07,708 --> 00:05:09,708
If I hadn’t moved fast, she’d have cut it off!

125
00:05:09,708 --> 00:05:11,500
She’d have cut it off!

126
00:05:11,500 --> 00:05:13,958
If she had, she’d have ruined herself!

127
00:05:13,958 --> 00:05:16,208
A man on a branch was sawing at its base…

128
00:05:16,208 --> 00:05:18,958
The orchard’s owner looked and saw.

129
00:05:18,958 --> 00:05:21,250
Dustali, talk sense, what did she want to cut? (He groans)

130
00:05:21,333 --> 00:05:22,625
I saw it myself!

131
00:05:22,708 --> 00:05:23,583
I saw it myself!

132
00:05:23,583 --> 00:05:25,750
The kitchen knife… - Go on!

133
00:05:25,750 --> 00:05:28,333
She’d brought it to bed! - Well?!

134
00:05:28,333 --> 00:05:30,208
She actually grabbed it to cut!

135
00:05:30,250 --> 00:05:32,625
Ay cut… cut

136
00:05:33,166 --> 00:05:34,291
Come, let’s take a look,

137
00:05:34,291 --> 00:05:35,666
Maybe she really did cut it off!

138
00:05:35,666 --> 00:05:36,541
Brother!

139
00:05:36,541 --> 00:05:37,416
Moment!

140
00:05:37,833 --> 00:05:39,583
It’s disgraceful, Shazdeh!- Moment you too

141
00:05:39,666 --> 00:05:41,666
Ugh, don’t you see he fainted again!

142
00:05:41,708 --> 00:05:43,916
Sir, Sir, come forward.

143
00:05:44,458 --> 00:05:46,333
This poor guy fainted again!

144
00:05:46,416 --> 00:05:48,291
Take a look, maybe she really did cut it off!

145
00:05:48,291 --> 00:05:48,916
Huh!

146
00:05:50,333 --> 00:05:51,041
Ghasem!

147
00:05:53,458 --> 00:05:54,208
Yes, Sir?

148
00:05:54,208 --> 00:05:55,208
Go take a look,

149
00:05:55,208 --> 00:05:57,583
See if she really cut it off or not!

150
00:05:57,708 --> 00:06:00,083
Yes, sir! - Why all this shouting and screaming? He’s examining!

151
00:06:00,083 --> 00:06:02,708
Ladies and kids, over there!

152
00:06:02,708 --> 00:06:03,708
Over there!

153
00:06:03,750 --> 00:06:04,500
- Over there.

154
00:06:04,500 --> 00:06:05,125
- Go, Sir.

155
00:06:05,125 --> 00:06:06,000
- You fainted again.

156
00:06:06,083 --> 00:06:07,583
(He groans)

157
00:06:07,625 --> 00:06:10,083
Do something to bring him round. (He groans)

158
00:06:10,083 --> 00:06:11,583
Butcher! Butcher… - Dustali!

159
00:06:12,875 --> 00:06:13,583
Ghasem…

160
00:06:14,208 --> 00:06:14,708
Cut!

161
00:06:15,458 --> 00:06:15,875
Cut!

162
00:06:16,625 --> 00:06:17,083
Cut!

163
00:06:17,375 --> 00:06:18,750
Honestly, Sir, why should I lie?

164
00:06:18,833 --> 00:06:20,958
The grave is this close!

165
00:06:21,041 --> 00:06:23,166
Seems the only cut was his circumcision!

166
00:06:23,208 --> 00:06:25,166
Sir, if you ask me,

167
00:06:25,208 --> 00:06:26,541
Nothing’s missing at all!

168
00:06:28,250 --> 00:06:31,125
What times we live in!

169
00:06:34,750 --> 00:06:35,333
We…

170
00:06:36,750 --> 00:06:39,000
A thousand times in wars,

171
00:06:40,375 --> 00:06:41,000
With,

172
00:06:41,541 --> 00:06:42,500
Rifle,

173
00:06:42,500 --> 00:06:43,916
Bayonet,

174
00:06:43,916 --> 00:06:45,041
Sword,

175
00:06:45,041 --> 00:06:46,125
Shrapnel,

176
00:06:46,166 --> 00:06:47,500
We came face to face…

177
00:06:48,125 --> 00:06:49,250
Never,

178
00:06:49,250 --> 00:06:51,500
Did fear enter our heart!

179
00:06:51,500 --> 00:06:51,875
Yes—

180
00:06:51,875 --> 00:06:53,500
God bless, Sir has the heart of a lion!

181
00:06:53,875 --> 00:06:56,291
Sir, remember the Boyr-Ahmadi war?

182
00:06:56,625 --> 00:06:58,500
There Mohammad, cleaver in hand,

183
00:06:58,500 --> 00:07:00,625
Leapt at you from his horse!

184
00:07:01,958 --> 00:07:02,875
Now…

185
00:07:03,583 --> 00:07:06,458
These people see a kitchen knife,

186
00:07:06,458 --> 00:07:08,000
Start shouting and screaming and…

187
00:07:08,083 --> 00:07:09,250
Faint! - Mash Ghasem!

188
00:07:09,333 --> 00:07:10,208
Come help!

189
00:07:10,250 --> 00:07:10,708
Come.

190
00:07:10,750 --> 00:07:11,833
Yes, Mr. Colonel, yes.

191
00:07:12,333 --> 00:07:14,458
And nothing of his even got cut!

192
00:07:14,458 --> 00:07:15,875
What would he do if it had!

193
00:07:15,958 --> 00:07:17,583
Yes, Sir, Mash Ghasem is right… he is right—

194
00:07:17,583 --> 00:07:20,000
Take him downstairs, maybe he’ll feel better.

195
00:07:22,250 --> 00:07:24,583
Easy, son… ah… careful.

196
00:07:29,791 --> 00:07:31,666
Mr. Dustali-Khan! - Go, go!

197
00:07:31,958 --> 00:07:33,291
Cut!… Cut!

198
00:07:33,291 --> 00:07:35,291
Why are you talking nonsense, Dustali!

199
00:07:35,458 --> 00:07:37,333
Is Lady Aziz-Saltaneh crazy!

200
00:07:37,416 --> 00:07:38,416
You’re imagining things!

201
00:07:38,416 --> 00:07:41,291
Help me! - Oh, be quiet, man!

202
00:07:41,291 --> 00:07:42,958
You ruined our reputation!

203
00:07:43,416 --> 00:07:45,916
First she picked a huge fight with me…

204
00:07:46,166 --> 00:07:47,416
She didn’t come to the ceremony either!

205
00:07:47,833 --> 00:07:49,666
Then she went into the kitchen,

206
00:07:49,666 --> 00:07:50,833
And sharpened it!

207
00:07:50,833 --> 00:07:53,041
Ouch!

208
00:07:53,541 --> 00:07:54,916
Someone from your family

209
00:07:54,958 --> 00:07:58,416
Told her I’m having an affair with a young woman!

210
00:07:58,458 --> 00:07:59,916
(He screams and groans)

211
00:07:59,916 --> 00:08:00,916
What!? What!?

212
00:08:00,916 --> 00:08:02,166
What did Dustali say!?

213
00:08:02,166 --> 00:08:03,916
Someone from our family!?

214
00:08:04,291 --> 00:08:06,583
To hell with a family like that!

215
00:08:06,583 --> 00:08:08,291
They’re all murderers!

216
00:08:08,583 --> 00:08:10,291
If I’d been any slower,

217
00:08:10,291 --> 00:08:11,541
She’d have cut it right off!

218
00:08:11,583 --> 00:08:13,583
(He screams and groans)

219
00:08:13,666 --> 00:08:17,458
Quiet! Quiet, Dustali! (He screams and groans)

220
00:08:17,458 --> 00:08:19,791
Now I see!

221
00:08:20,333 --> 00:08:25,083
I know which vile man is behind this!

222
00:08:25,541 --> 00:08:26,458
That man,

223
00:08:26,458 --> 00:08:30,541
Wants to damage our family’s honor!

224
00:08:30,541 --> 00:08:34,958
He has conspired against our family’s honor!

225
00:08:35,041 --> 00:08:37,791
I’ll make him pay!

226
00:08:37,833 --> 00:08:42,166
My family’s honor is no joking matter!

227
00:08:42,208 --> 00:08:43,791
This man knows,

228
00:08:43,791 --> 00:08:46,958
That Dustali is my weak spot!

229
00:08:47,041 --> 00:08:51,166
He knows that I raised Dustali from childhood!

230
00:08:51,166 --> 00:08:54,041
He is like my own child!

231
00:08:54,041 --> 00:08:56,541
He’s my relative!

232
00:08:56,541 --> 00:08:59,166
His wife is my relative!

233
00:08:59,166 --> 00:09:00,666
They sure have patience!

234
00:09:01,541 --> 00:09:03,541
They’re about to go at each other again.

235
00:09:05,166 --> 00:09:06,166
Farrokh Lagha Khanom!

236
00:09:06,416 --> 00:09:09,208
I wish I could die and be done with this life.

237
00:09:10,833 --> 00:09:13,416
I had hoped that when the kids grew up,

238
00:09:14,041 --> 00:09:16,208
When Saeid turned twenty

239
00:09:16,541 --> 00:09:17,916
Finished his studies,

240
00:09:17,958 --> 00:09:19,791
I’d marry Leili to Saeid.

241
00:09:19,791 --> 00:09:23,291
(She cries)

242
00:09:26,916 --> 00:09:28,666
This is all his doing!

243
00:09:28,666 --> 00:09:30,333
He wants to set everyone against each other!

244
00:09:30,916 --> 00:09:32,166
There is no doubt,

245
00:09:32,166 --> 00:09:35,083
That vile man told Aziz-Saltaneh!

246
00:09:35,083 --> 00:09:36,916
Napoleon’s strategy,

247
00:09:36,958 --> 00:09:39,666
Which he heard from me over backgammon,

248
00:09:39,666 --> 00:09:41,166
Now he’s using it against me!

249
00:09:42,291 --> 00:09:43,666
Napoleon,

250
00:09:43,791 --> 00:09:46,291
Says that in war, you must always

251
00:09:46,333 --> 00:09:49,666
Attack the enemy’s weakest point.

252
00:09:49,833 --> 00:09:53,333
And now he’s attacked my family honor!

253
00:09:53,416 --> 00:09:55,541
I’ll make you pay! Now, don’t get angry!

254
00:09:55,541 --> 00:09:57,083
- Maybe it’s not his work!

255
00:09:57,166 --> 00:09:58,916
- Don’t rush to judgment.

256
00:10:05,166 --> 00:10:06,916
First the investigation,

257
00:10:07,041 --> 00:10:08,041
Then the verdict!

258
00:10:11,666 --> 00:10:13,583
Eh… Mr. Dustali-Khan?

259
00:10:13,833 --> 00:10:16,291
Please, with complete precision,

260
00:10:16,791 --> 00:10:17,916
And honesty,

261
00:10:17,958 --> 00:10:19,916
Answer my questions.

262
00:10:20,291 --> 00:10:22,541
Is this any time for an interrogation?

263
00:10:22,916 --> 00:10:25,541
Brother Khan, leave this for tomorrow.

264
00:10:25,708 --> 00:10:28,291
Don’t you see this poor guy fainted!

265
00:10:28,291 --> 00:10:30,333
He doesn’t have the strength to speak!

266
00:10:30,541 --> 00:10:31,833
It’s midnight!

267
00:10:31,958 --> 00:10:33,458
The best time,

268
00:10:33,541 --> 00:10:35,916
For interrogation and investigation,

269
00:10:36,291 --> 00:10:38,791
Is right after the crime!

270
00:10:38,916 --> 00:10:41,416
By tomorrow, the evidence

271
00:10:41,458 --> 00:10:42,666
Will be scattered!

272
00:10:43,333 --> 00:10:44,291
Yes, Sir!

273
00:10:44,291 --> 00:10:46,666
Who knows who’ll be alive tomorrow!

274
00:10:47,166 --> 00:10:48,791
We had a fellow villager…

275
00:10:48,916 --> 00:10:50,041
He was alive at night,

276
00:10:50,208 --> 00:10:51,291
The next morning he was dead!

277
00:10:51,333 --> 00:10:52,583
Mash Ghasem!

278
00:10:53,166 --> 00:10:53,958
Mr. Colonel,

279
00:10:54,041 --> 00:10:56,083
Please sit down so we can begin.

280
00:10:56,916 --> 00:10:58,916
God give me patience!

281
00:11:03,166 --> 00:11:03,916
Dustali!

282
00:11:04,416 --> 00:11:05,541
In gratitude,

283
00:11:05,541 --> 00:11:08,458
For all the care I’ve always shown you,

284
00:11:08,541 --> 00:11:09,583
I ask you

285
00:11:09,666 --> 00:11:10,833
To answer, precisely,

286
00:11:11,166 --> 00:11:14,666
Shamsali Mirza’s questions.

287
00:11:15,083 --> 00:11:17,916
Tonight the truth must be discovered.

288
00:11:18,666 --> 00:11:21,583
Just as it is clear to me,

289
00:11:21,833 --> 00:11:25,166
It must become clear to everyone

290
00:11:25,208 --> 00:11:27,666
Who slandered you!

291
00:11:28,416 --> 00:11:29,291
Who,

292
00:11:29,291 --> 00:11:31,333
Told Aziz-Saltaneh

293
00:11:31,333 --> 00:11:33,416
That you’re having an affair with a woman!

294
00:11:33,958 --> 00:11:35,166
We are now

295
00:11:35,166 --> 00:11:38,208
In the most sensitive moments,

296
00:11:38,291 --> 00:11:42,541
Of our family’s history.

297
00:11:42,666 --> 00:11:46,083
We are on the verge of collapse.

298
00:11:46,208 --> 00:11:50,791
Our family honor is in danger!

299
00:11:51,291 --> 00:11:55,041
Especially my sister must understand,

300
00:11:55,083 --> 00:11:58,666
What kind of man she’s living with!

301
00:12:05,333 --> 00:12:06,458
Before the interrogation,

302
00:12:06,458 --> 00:12:08,583
By your leave, Your Excellency!

303
00:12:08,958 --> 00:12:10,791
Ladies and children,

304
00:12:10,833 --> 00:12:12,541
Everyone go home.

305
00:12:13,208 --> 00:12:13,916
Leili!

306
00:12:14,958 --> 00:12:15,583
Home.

307
00:12:21,458 --> 00:12:21,916
Saeid!

308
00:12:30,583 --> 00:12:31,333
Home!

309
00:12:32,166 --> 00:12:34,166
Only my sister stays.

310
00:12:35,083 --> 00:12:36,916
She must stay,

311
00:12:36,916 --> 00:12:39,333
So she can choose between

312
00:12:39,416 --> 00:12:40,541
Her husband and her family!

313
00:12:40,541 --> 00:12:42,166
Brother Khan! - Quiet!

314
00:12:43,791 --> 00:12:45,458
Lady Farrokh Lagha, if you please.

315
00:12:45,541 --> 00:12:46,791
And why me?!

316
00:12:47,208 --> 00:12:49,916
My dear lady, this is no place for you!

317
00:12:50,083 --> 00:12:51,916
How come it’s a place for your sister!

318
00:12:51,958 --> 00:12:53,291
It’s no place for me?

319
00:12:53,541 --> 00:12:56,916
My sister is an interested party here!

320
00:12:57,041 --> 00:12:57,916
Let me see!

321
00:12:57,916 --> 00:12:59,041
Aziz-Saltaneh wanted

322
00:12:59,041 --> 00:13:01,083
To cut off a part of Dustali-Khan’s body,

323
00:13:01,166 --> 00:13:03,541
And your sister is an interested party?

324
00:13:03,541 --> 00:13:04,416
Yes!

325
00:13:04,458 --> 00:13:05,041
Moment!

326
00:13:05,041 --> 00:13:07,041
All ladies are interested parties!

327
00:13:07,041 --> 00:13:09,916
This incident is painful for all womankind!

328
00:13:10,166 --> 00:13:11,541
Get lost, you clown!

329
00:13:11,583 --> 00:13:12,166
Shazdeh!

330
00:13:14,166 --> 00:13:15,291
Poori, home!

331
00:13:23,166 --> 00:13:26,666
(They whisper)

332
00:13:26,666 --> 00:13:29,541
Lord save us from the sharp tongues of these women!

333
00:13:29,541 --> 00:13:32,041
Please proceed, Your Excellency!

334
00:13:33,458 --> 00:13:34,958
Mr. Dustali-Khan,

335
00:13:34,958 --> 00:13:37,041
State your identity…

336
00:13:37,041 --> 00:13:38,833
S… s… sorry

337
00:13:39,041 --> 00:13:40,291
I mean,

338
00:13:40,333 --> 00:13:42,916
Describe the details of the event.

339
00:13:42,916 --> 00:13:44,416
What details!

340
00:13:44,416 --> 00:13:46,166
She was cutting it, that’s all…

341
00:13:46,208 --> 00:13:47,458
Sir!

342
00:13:48,083 --> 00:13:50,541
Tell me exactly when

343
00:13:50,541 --> 00:13:52,416
This incident happened?

344
00:13:52,916 --> 00:13:54,708
Tonight, of course!

345
00:13:54,833 --> 00:13:56,458
Mr. Dustali-Khan!

346
00:13:56,666 --> 00:13:59,416
I mean, exactly

347
00:13:59,416 --> 00:14:01,791
What time did it happen?

348
00:14:02,041 --> 00:14:03,166
Leave me alone, come on…

349
00:14:03,166 --> 00:14:04,791
Get off my back.

350
00:14:04,833 --> 00:14:06,166
What do I know, Sir!

351
00:14:06,208 --> 00:14:08,666
She’d grabbed it to cut, that’s all!

352
00:14:09,083 --> 00:14:10,458
My dear sir!

353
00:14:10,833 --> 00:14:14,041
You were the target of an assassination attempt.

354
00:14:14,208 --> 00:14:17,083
When fate brings pain to one limb,

355
00:14:17,208 --> 00:14:19,291
The other limbs cannot rest.

356
00:14:19,291 --> 00:14:20,083
- Quiet!

357
00:14:21,416 --> 00:14:22,583
The accused

358
00:14:22,666 --> 00:14:23,958
Intended

359
00:14:24,041 --> 00:14:26,458
To cut off a noble member

360
00:14:26,458 --> 00:14:27,416
Of your body!

361
00:14:27,416 --> 00:14:29,333
And you don’t know what time it was?

362
00:14:29,333 --> 00:14:30,416
Moment! Moment

363
00:14:30,458 --> 00:14:31,333
Brother Khan

364
00:14:31,416 --> 00:14:33,208
Dustali-Khan wasn’t wearing a watch

365
00:14:33,291 --> 00:14:35,041
On his noble member!

366
00:14:35,041 --> 00:14:36,791
You are mocking me? -Moment!

367
00:14:36,791 --> 00:14:39,291
You’re mocking me, you shameless man?

368
00:14:39,291 --> 00:14:41,083
Now you’re mocking me too?

369
00:14:41,166 --> 00:14:42,916
I’ll go tell him now,

370
00:14:42,916 --> 00:14:45,208
He’ll come teach you a lesson!

371
00:14:45,208 --> 00:14:46,708
Why did Farrokh Lagha Khanom do that?!

372
00:14:47,541 --> 00:14:49,041
I didn’t say anything to her!

373
00:14:49,166 --> 00:14:49,666
What do you mean!

374
00:14:49,666 --> 00:14:51,666
(The Colonel laughs)

375
00:14:51,666 --> 00:14:54,041
Well, “Noble” is her son-in-law’s surname.

376
00:14:54,041 --> 00:14:55,291
(Crowd laughter)

377
00:14:55,291 --> 00:14:56,291
Quiet. (Crowd laughter)

378
00:14:56,333 --> 00:14:57,458
(Crowd laughter)

379
00:14:57,541 --> 00:14:58,791
Quiet.

380
00:14:58,833 --> 00:15:00,166
(Crowd laughter)

381
00:15:00,208 --> 00:15:01,666
Ghasem, shut up!

382
00:15:02,083 --> 00:15:04,875
(They laugh quietly)

383
00:15:07,541 --> 00:15:08,208
Very well!

384
00:15:08,291 --> 00:15:10,541
Then, with the gentlemen’s permission,

385
00:15:10,541 --> 00:15:12,416
From this merry gathering,

386
00:15:12,416 --> 00:15:13,291
I’ll take my leave.

387
00:15:13,291 --> 00:15:15,916
Please, Your Excellency, stay.

388
00:15:15,916 --> 00:15:17,208
Please, sit.

389
00:15:17,208 --> 00:15:18,208
She’s a foul-mouthed woman.

390
00:15:18,333 --> 00:15:19,916
Good thing she left.

391
00:15:20,166 --> 00:15:22,208
Please, do continue.

392
00:15:23,166 --> 00:15:24,458
Brother, quiet.

393
00:15:24,541 --> 00:15:25,541
Ghasem!

394
00:15:26,083 --> 00:15:29,583
(They laugh quietly)

395
00:15:47,500 --> 00:15:49,375
Mr. Dustali-Khan!

396
00:15:50,250 --> 00:15:53,375
Please answer my second question.

397
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:57,416
Was the knife a regular knife or a pocketknife?

398
00:15:57,625 --> 00:15:59,625
It was a kitchen knife!

399
00:15:59,625 --> 00:16:01,375
Oh!

400
00:16:01,416 --> 00:16:04,250
Which hand was she holding the knife in?

401
00:16:04,625 --> 00:16:06,375
Honestly, Sir, why should I lie!

402
00:16:07,416 --> 00:16:09,166
As far as we remember,

403
00:16:09,250 --> 00:16:11,791
Butchers, when they… - Butcher… butcher…

404
00:16:11,875 --> 00:16:13,416
Butchers, when they cut,

405
00:16:13,416 --> 00:16:15,166
Hold the knife in their right hand.

406
00:16:15,250 --> 00:16:17,416
Let him answer himself, Sir!

407
00:16:18,375 --> 00:16:20,375
Yes… yes…

408
00:16:21,125 --> 00:16:24,000
Apparently the knife was in her right hand.

409
00:16:24,125 --> 00:16:25,666
What was in her left hand?

410
00:16:25,666 --> 00:16:26,666
Moment! Moment

411
00:16:26,750 --> 00:16:28,875
Her left hand was probably holding the noble member!

412
00:16:28,875 --> 00:16:29,250
Brother!

413
00:16:29,250 --> 00:16:34,125
(Crowd laughter)

414
00:16:34,125 --> 00:16:35,541
Brother Khan, I’m going home.

415
00:16:35,541 --> 00:16:36,875
There’s a limit to everything!

416
00:16:36,875 --> 00:16:39,000
I asked you to stay!

417
00:16:39,041 --> 00:16:39,791
Yes, lady.

418
00:16:39,875 --> 00:16:41,625
Please stay until things become clear.

419
00:16:41,625 --> 00:16:42,375
Please, sit.

420
00:16:43,125 --> 00:16:43,916
Brother Khan.

421
00:16:44,041 --> 00:16:44,625
Please, sit.

422
00:16:44,875 --> 00:16:46,000
Mr. Dustali Khan.

423
00:16:46,250 --> 00:16:47,291
Pay attention.

424
00:16:47,500 --> 00:16:50,125
This question is very important.

425
00:16:50,666 --> 00:16:54,000
Tonight, you and Lady Aziz-Saltaneh…

426
00:16:56,250 --> 00:16:59,166
I must declare the session closed.

427
00:16:59,250 --> 00:17:01,875
Closed? What do you mean, Your Excellency! We’re not strangers.

428
00:17:02,750 --> 00:17:03,166
Lady.

429
00:17:03,625 --> 00:17:06,541
Guess what they’re talking about?

430
00:17:06,625 --> 00:17:07,541
Sister!

431
00:17:07,541 --> 00:17:08,250
Sister!

432
00:17:09,541 --> 00:17:10,916
I beg my sister

433
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:12,750
To step over there for a minute.

434
00:17:12,791 --> 00:17:15,125
Sister, please go over there for a minute,

435
00:17:15,125 --> 00:17:16,166
Then come back.

436
00:17:16,750 --> 00:17:17,250
Brother Khan,

437
00:17:17,291 --> 00:17:18,500
I’m going home.

438
00:17:19,541 --> 00:17:21,041
Sister, I said,

439
00:17:21,041 --> 00:17:23,125
Stay here for a minute.

440
00:17:23,916 --> 00:17:25,375
- What a situation!

441
00:17:29,291 --> 00:17:30,250
Mr. Dustali-Khan!

442
00:17:30,291 --> 00:17:32,916
Tonight, you and Lady Aziz-Saltaneh…

443
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:33,875
In bed…

444
00:17:33,875 --> 00:17:35,291
Let go of me, Sir!

445
00:17:35,375 --> 00:17:37,041
With that old hag…

446
00:17:37,041 --> 00:17:39,125
Haven’t you seen what my wife looks like!

447
00:17:39,125 --> 00:17:40,750
I bet this question,

448
00:17:40,750 --> 00:17:42,250
Was about San Francisco.

449
00:17:42,291 --> 00:17:44,166
There’s a limit to everything, Shazdeh!

450
00:17:44,250 --> 00:17:46,375
I said you must be here!

451
00:17:46,416 --> 00:17:48,625
This childish behavior is disgraceful!

452
00:17:52,833 --> 00:17:54,125
Your Excellency…

453
00:17:54,458 --> 00:17:56,083
Basically, the matter

454
00:17:56,083 --> 00:17:57,500
Is something else.

455
00:17:57,958 --> 00:18:01,208
I want you to make this man confess

456
00:18:01,208 --> 00:18:01,958
Who,

457
00:18:02,333 --> 00:18:05,875
Told his wife about his affair with a young woman,

458
00:18:06,125 --> 00:18:08,208
Who told her!

459
00:18:08,375 --> 00:18:10,958
You’re asking very strange questions!

460
00:18:11,250 --> 00:18:14,333
Then, Sir, you do the interrogating!

461
00:18:14,333 --> 00:18:15,500
I’ll take my leave.

462
00:18:16,958 --> 00:18:18,583
A judge should not stay

463
00:18:18,625 --> 00:18:21,333
Where his position

464
00:18:21,333 --> 00:18:22,375
Is not respected.

465
00:18:22,375 --> 00:18:23,708
Please, I beg you!

466
00:18:23,708 --> 00:18:24,958
I only wanted to clarify…

467
00:18:24,958 --> 00:18:26,583
Things for Your Excellency… - So this wretch came over here!

468
00:18:26,583 --> 00:18:27,458
Oh, dear God…

469
00:18:27,500 --> 00:18:28,833
Running away from me?

470
00:18:28,833 --> 00:18:31,750
Help me! - Damn your ugly face!

471
00:18:31,833 --> 00:18:32,958
Quick, go back home!

472
00:18:32,958 --> 00:18:34,333
(Dustali groans from fear)

473
00:18:34,333 --> 00:18:35,625
Now I’ll burn your beard!

474
00:18:35,708 --> 00:18:36,250
She’s coming here!

475
00:18:36,250 --> 00:18:37,708
She’s coming here, help me! - Quick, get up!

476
00:18:37,708 --> 00:18:38,875
I beg you, Mash Ghasem! - Get up, I said!

477
00:18:38,958 --> 00:18:40,125
I beg you. - I’ll chop you to bits!

478
00:18:40,208 --> 00:18:42,083
Hide me somewhere, Mash Ghasem!

479
00:18:42,083 --> 00:18:43,583
I beg you, Mash Ghasem! - Don’t be scared, Sir is here!

480
00:18:43,583 --> 00:18:44,458
Sir!

481
00:18:44,458 --> 00:18:46,458
What a scandal you’ve caused!

482
00:18:46,458 --> 00:18:48,625
Don’t let her come… don’t let her come down - Get up, you lazy lump.

483
00:18:48,625 --> 00:18:50,125
I’m scared of this battle-axe.

484
00:18:50,208 --> 00:18:52,083
What kind of game is this!

485
00:18:52,125 --> 00:18:53,375
I’ll give him hell!

486
00:18:53,458 --> 00:18:54,083
I’ll kill him!

487
00:18:54,125 --> 00:18:56,083
Take that ladder out from under her - He wishes!

488
00:18:56,083 --> 00:18:57,583
Damn you, you wretch!

489
00:18:57,583 --> 00:18:59,333
Lady Aziz-Saltaneh… - Damn you!

490
00:18:59,375 --> 00:19:00,708
- Please! - Come out! - Hold him!

491
00:19:00,875 --> 00:19:03,958
Lady, please be quiet! (Crowd noise)

492
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:05,583
Lady Aziz-Saltaneh! - I’ll kill the bastard!

493
00:19:05,625 --> 00:19:09,458
Please be quiet, lady! - Let me see what happened!

494
00:19:09,458 --> 00:19:10,583
What business is it of yours anyway? - Calm down!

495
00:19:10,583 --> 00:19:11,875
Is he my husband or yours?

496
00:19:11,958 --> 00:19:12,833
Let go of me! - Lady!

497
00:19:12,833 --> 00:19:14,875
Oh Imam Ali, save me!

498
00:19:14,958 --> 00:19:16,375
She’s going to kill me…

499
00:19:16,458 --> 00:19:17,833
Lady Aziz-Saltaneh…

500
00:19:17,833 --> 00:19:20,833
The honor and dignity of an aristocratic family,

501
00:19:20,833 --> 00:19:22,458
Is in danger! - To hell with danger!

502
00:19:22,458 --> 00:19:23,958
Who said he’s having an affair with another man’s wife?

503
00:19:23,958 --> 00:19:25,000
Ask the damned man himself!

504
00:19:25,083 --> 00:19:26,750
Ask that leering lecher himself!

505
00:19:26,750 --> 00:19:27,708
Lady Aziz-Saltaneh!

506
00:19:27,708 --> 00:19:31,708
Can you tell me who told you

507
00:19:31,750 --> 00:19:34,458
About Dustali’s affair with a young woman?

508
00:19:34,500 --> 00:19:35,708
Whoever said it was right!

509
00:19:35,708 --> 00:19:36,583
It’s the truth!

510
00:19:36,583 --> 00:19:38,083
Shameless! Shameless! - Take the cleaver from her!

511
00:19:38,083 --> 00:19:39,708
For a year he’s been saying I’m tired,

512
00:19:39,708 --> 00:19:40,583
I’m sick!

513
00:19:40,583 --> 00:19:41,458
I’m this!

514
00:19:41,500 --> 00:19:42,208
I’m that!

515
00:19:42,250 --> 00:19:43,208
I’m the other!

516
00:19:43,208 --> 00:19:45,208
Then he went with Shir-Ali the butcher’s wife!

517
00:19:45,208 --> 00:19:46,208
With whose wife?

518
00:19:46,208 --> 00:19:46,958
Shir-Ali!

519
00:19:46,958 --> 00:19:49,625
Oh no… don’t let him hear!

520
00:19:49,625 --> 00:19:50,333
Moment!

521
00:19:50,333 --> 00:19:51,833
Moment!

522
00:19:51,833 --> 00:19:53,833
I can’t believe it!

523
00:19:53,875 --> 00:19:55,958
I’ll kill him and destroy myself too! - Let me see, let me see!

524
00:19:55,958 --> 00:19:57,250
This cowardly dishonorable Dustali, - Be patient!

525
00:19:57,250 --> 00:19:59,500
Went to San Francisco with Shir-Ali’s wife!?

526
00:19:59,500 --> 00:20:00,333
I hope you drop dead!

527
00:20:00,375 --> 00:20:02,833
Bravo, bravo, dear lady!

528
00:20:03,083 --> 00:20:04,708
- It would’ve been a shame to cut off his family jewels!

529
00:20:04,708 --> 00:20:06,208
Honestly, if I were you,

530
00:20:06,208 --> 00:20:08,333
I would kill you!

531
00:20:08,333 --> 00:20:09,708
I’d buy his member a watch as a prize.

532
00:20:09,708 --> 00:20:10,708
Ugh!… Moment…

533
00:20:11,708 --> 00:20:13,458
Lady! Moment!

534
00:20:13,458 --> 00:20:14,500
Why point your knife at me? - Be patient a minute!

535
00:20:15,083 --> 00:20:16,000
At my throat!

536
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:17,583
Your big jackass of a husband

537
00:20:17,583 --> 00:20:19,083
Went to San Francisco with Shir-Ali’s wife,

538
00:20:19,083 --> 00:20:20,125
And you pull a knife on me?

539
00:20:20,208 --> 00:20:21,250
Lazy bum! - Let go, Sir!

540
00:20:21,250 --> 00:20:22,375
None of our business! - I’ll set you on fire!

541
00:20:22,458 --> 00:20:24,083
It’s between you,

542
00:20:24,125 --> 00:20:25,458
The kitchen knife,

543
00:20:25,750 --> 00:20:27,208
And donkey Dustali’s family jewels!

544
00:20:27,208 --> 00:20:28,583
Hey Shir-Ali!

545
00:20:28,583 --> 00:20:30,375
I’m begging you, Asdollah!

546
00:20:30,375 --> 00:20:32,458
Stop saying that bastard’s name!

547
00:20:32,458 --> 00:20:32,958
Come on, my life is in danger!

548
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:34,208
Shameless!

549
00:20:34,208 --> 00:20:35,083
When you went into his wife’s arms,

550
00:20:35,083 --> 00:20:36,208
Your life wasn’t in danger!

551
00:20:36,208 --> 00:20:38,000
Son of a bitch! - All right!

552
00:20:38,208 --> 00:20:39,833
Let go of me! - Have mercy, lady!

553
00:20:39,833 --> 00:20:41,958
Just tell me,

554
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:43,125
Who told you

555
00:20:43,208 --> 00:20:45,125
That this idiot,

556
00:20:45,208 --> 00:20:46,000
With that big jackass’s wife, - Damn him!

557
00:20:46,083 --> 00:20:48,458
Is having an affair?

558
00:20:48,458 --> 00:20:49,833
I can’t say, I can’t!

559
00:20:49,875 --> 00:20:51,333
By the soul of the late Great Sir,

560
00:20:51,333 --> 00:20:53,458
Don’t let her near me!

561
00:20:53,458 --> 00:20:54,333
I’m scared of this battle-axe!

562
00:20:54,333 --> 00:20:55,458
Who told you?

563
00:20:55,458 --> 00:20:55,833
I said I can’t say!

564
00:20:55,833 --> 00:20:57,458
No!

565
00:20:57,500 --> 00:20:58,375
Lady, - I can’t!

566
00:20:58,458 --> 00:20:59,875
Out of respect

567
00:20:59,958 --> 00:21:02,708
For the honor of a great family, - I can’t say!

568
00:21:02,708 --> 00:21:05,000
In the name of your son-in-law’s honor, - I can’t say… I can’t!

569
00:21:05,083 --> 00:21:06,750
Please… - To hell with my husband’s honor!

570
00:21:07,125 --> 00:21:08,875
Lady Aziz-Saltaneh!

571
00:21:08,958 --> 00:21:10,583
Oh, she’s killing me…

572
00:21:10,583 --> 00:21:11,958
Oh, she’s killing me…

573
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:14,458
To hell with you and your honor…

574
00:21:14,458 --> 00:21:15,625
(She starts crying)

575
00:21:15,625 --> 00:21:19,125
I never want a husband again as long as I live.

576
00:21:20,125 --> 00:21:21,958
Tomorrow I’ll go sit down

577
00:21:21,958 --> 00:21:24,125
And tell Shir-Ali all of it.

578
00:21:24,208 --> 00:21:25,333
Then let’s see if there’s a husband left

579
00:21:25,333 --> 00:21:26,875
To cheat on me!

580
00:21:26,875 --> 00:21:29,833
No lady… no don’t do this!

581
00:21:31,708 --> 00:21:34,458
Your life will be in danger!

582
00:21:35,083 --> 00:21:36,583
This Shir-Ali, this guy…

583
00:21:37,083 --> 00:21:39,083
If, so far,

584
00:21:39,083 --> 00:21:42,208
He hasn’t found out about his wife’s affairs,

585
00:21:42,250 --> 00:21:43,458
The reason is,

586
00:21:43,458 --> 00:21:46,833
No one dares to go tell him!

587
00:21:48,583 --> 00:21:50,500
Take our own servant Ghasem!

588
00:21:51,083 --> 00:21:51,750
Last year,

589
00:21:51,750 --> 00:21:54,750
He said just one thing to him: Shir-Ali,

590
00:21:54,750 --> 00:21:56,333
Watch your wife!

591
00:21:56,750 --> 00:21:57,875
Then…

592
00:21:57,958 --> 00:21:59,833
A whole week,

593
00:21:59,833 --> 00:22:02,208
He left his shop,

594
00:22:02,333 --> 00:22:04,000
Cleaver in hand,

595
00:22:04,083 --> 00:22:06,750
Came and sat outside our front door.

596
00:22:07,708 --> 00:22:09,083
Isn’t that right, Ghasem!

597
00:22:09,083 --> 00:22:09,500
Huh?

598
00:22:09,583 --> 00:22:10,625
Get up and come here! - Yes, Sir, yes!

599
00:22:10,708 --> 00:22:12,375
He’ll tell you himself. - Sir has summoned me!

600
00:22:12,458 --> 00:22:14,125
You watch him - Okay, go my dear, go.

601
00:22:14,333 --> 00:22:15,250
No… no don’t go Mash Ghasem!

602
00:22:15,333 --> 00:22:15,833
Don’t go, for my sake!

603
00:22:15,833 --> 00:22:17,500
Calm down my dear, calm down! - Don’t go… don’t go!

604
00:22:17,583 --> 00:22:18,333
It’s not good!

605
00:22:18,375 --> 00:22:20,333
You want to go sit there? - Don’t go Mash Ghasem!

606
00:22:20,333 --> 00:22:21,958
Stay away from him? - Honestly, Sir, why should I lie!

607
00:22:21,958 --> 00:22:24,083
We didn’t even say that to him!

608
00:22:24,083 --> 00:22:25,000
We said,

609
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:27,250
Don’t let your wife go out of the house so much!

610
00:22:27,333 --> 00:22:29,083
We had no bad intention.

611
00:22:29,458 --> 00:22:31,958
Because a thief had come and taken his rug!

612
00:22:31,958 --> 00:22:34,625
We told him, don’t let your wife go out of the house,

613
00:22:34,625 --> 00:22:35,708
So no thief would come.

614
00:22:35,958 --> 00:22:37,625
And that godless man… - Go on!

615
00:22:38,125 --> 00:22:39,708
By the light of this lamp,

616
00:22:39,708 --> 00:22:40,458
No no!

617
00:22:40,500 --> 00:22:42,583
I swear by the light of that other lamp!

618
00:22:42,583 --> 00:22:43,958
From the bazaar arcade

619
00:22:43,958 --> 00:22:47,833
All the way to our door, he followed us with a cleaver!

620
00:22:48,833 --> 00:22:50,458
God bless Sir!

621
00:22:50,750 --> 00:22:52,125
God protect him.

622
00:22:52,583 --> 00:22:55,708
For ten, twenty full days,

623
00:22:55,708 --> 00:22:57,125
Rifle in hand,

624
00:22:57,125 --> 00:22:58,958
Watched over us. - He fainted… fainted!

625
00:22:58,958 --> 00:23:01,125
Oh, he fainted and fell… - Fainted… yes!

626
00:23:01,125 --> 00:23:02,208
Move aside, Mash Ghasem!

627
00:23:02,208 --> 00:23:03,833
That poor guy fainted!

628
00:23:03,958 --> 00:23:05,083
My dear lady!

629
00:23:05,375 --> 00:23:06,458
If I,

630
00:23:06,500 --> 00:23:10,000
God is my witness, even if I saw with my own eyes

631
00:23:10,083 --> 00:23:12,083
That this wretched Dustali

632
00:23:12,125 --> 00:23:15,000
Was really up to something shameful,

633
00:23:15,333 --> 00:23:17,458
I wouldn’t believe it, I wouldn’t!

634
00:23:17,625 --> 00:23:19,458
This poor wretch,

635
00:23:19,750 --> 00:23:21,958
Hardly has the strength to breathe!

636
00:23:22,083 --> 00:23:23,708
Wait, what did you say? - Am I lying?

637
00:23:23,958 --> 00:23:26,083
So now Dustali’s an old cripple?

638
00:23:26,083 --> 00:23:27,750
And he can’t breathe anymore, huh?

639
00:23:27,833 --> 00:23:30,333
You tell me… how is that possible, how?

640
00:23:30,333 --> 00:23:31,250
Huh? How is it possible!

641
00:23:31,333 --> 00:23:32,833
If you had so much breath yourself,

642
00:23:32,833 --> 00:23:34,208
Your wife wouldn’t have done that to you,

643
00:23:34,250 --> 00:23:35,250
You self-satisfied bastard!

644
00:23:35,333 --> 00:23:37,083
Don’t you ever mention my wife again!

645
00:23:38,500 --> 00:23:42,250
(Lady Aziz-Saltaneh starts crying)

646
00:24:00,083 --> 00:24:02,083
No problem, brother.

647
00:24:02,333 --> 00:24:03,458
No problem.

648
00:24:19,833 --> 00:24:25,750
♪ Mahur piece – Yahya Zarpanjeh ♪

649
00:24:45,666 --> 00:24:46,625
Pencil sharpener.

650
00:24:46,625 --> 00:24:48,125
It had fallen on the ground.

651
00:24:57,791 --> 00:24:58,250
Shi…

652
00:24:58,625 --> 00:24:58,916
Shi…

653
00:24:59,750 --> 00:25:00,166
Shi…

654
00:25:00,666 --> 00:25:01,250
Shir…

655
00:25:02,750 --> 00:25:03,416
What happened?

656
00:25:05,500 --> 00:25:06,291
What happened?

657
00:25:06,375 --> 00:25:06,875
Shi…

658
00:25:06,916 --> 00:25:07,625
Shi…

659
00:25:07,916 --> 00:25:08,625
Shi…

660
00:25:09,500 --> 00:25:10,500
Shir…

661
00:25:15,625 --> 00:25:16,500
Shir…

662
00:25:18,041 --> 00:25:18,625
Shir…

663
00:25:19,250 --> 00:25:20,291
Shir-Ali!

664
00:25:21,375 --> 00:25:22,750
Brother Khan, Shir-Ali!

665
00:25:22,791 --> 00:25:23,875
Shi… shi… shi… shir…

666
00:25:23,875 --> 00:25:25,375
Mr. Shir-Ali!

667
00:25:25,416 --> 00:25:27,416
Just a few minutes ago,

668
00:25:27,625 --> 00:25:29,500
We were just speaking well of you!

669
00:25:29,500 --> 00:25:31,250
Sorry to drop in like this, Sir.

670
00:25:31,291 --> 00:25:33,791
We were asleep in the house when my wife said,

671
00:25:33,791 --> 00:25:35,750
Shir-Ali, seems they’re calling you.

672
00:25:37,750 --> 00:25:39,291
Suddenly we got worried,

673
00:25:39,291 --> 00:25:42,500
Maybe a thief had come to Sir’s house again!

674
00:25:42,875 --> 00:25:43,625
Because,

675
00:25:43,625 --> 00:25:46,291
Last time we caught the thief right there.

676
00:25:46,291 --> 00:25:49,125
We… were expecting you tonight!

677
00:25:49,291 --> 00:25:50,875
You didn’t come to the ceremony!

678
00:25:50,875 --> 00:25:52,791
May you always watch over us, Sir!

679
00:25:53,000 --> 00:25:54,791
We went to Shabdol-Azim.

680
00:25:54,791 --> 00:25:56,500
Well… a blessed pilgrimage!

681
00:25:56,500 --> 00:25:58,250
We didn’t go on pilgrimage!

682
00:25:58,291 --> 00:26:00,666
We went to settle accounts with

683
00:26:00,750 --> 00:26:02,666
Asghar the sheep-seller,

684
00:26:02,875 --> 00:26:04,750
Once and for all!

685
00:26:05,000 --> 00:26:06,416
Pardon the mention, Sir,

686
00:26:06,416 --> 00:26:07,875
If you’ll excuse me,

687
00:26:07,875 --> 00:26:11,500
The bastard had sold us a sick sheep!

688
00:26:11,875 --> 00:26:14,250
I hope you got your money back?

689
00:26:14,250 --> 00:26:15,666
Of course, Sir!

690
00:26:15,750 --> 00:26:18,666
At first he hemmed and hawed, of course.

691
00:26:19,791 --> 00:26:23,000
With the carcass of that same dead sheep,

692
00:26:23,000 --> 00:26:25,416
We gave him a couple of whacks,

693
00:26:25,500 --> 00:26:28,041
Not only did we get the money,

694
00:26:28,041 --> 00:26:30,125
We got our travel fare too.

695
00:26:30,791 --> 00:26:32,875
So what was wrong with it, Shir-Ali?

696
00:26:32,875 --> 00:26:34,500
We don’t know, Sir!

697
00:26:34,541 --> 00:26:36,416
Seems it was sick!

698
00:26:37,250 --> 00:26:38,666
Pardon me, Sir,

699
00:26:38,750 --> 00:26:40,541
It was all bloated.

700
00:26:40,541 --> 00:26:41,750
Ugh… Mr. Shir-Ali? - Yes?

701
00:26:42,125 --> 00:26:44,125
Anyway thank you very much,

702
00:26:44,125 --> 00:26:45,916
That you always think of us.

703
00:26:46,625 --> 00:26:48,000
Shir-Ali!

704
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:52,000
Sir is kind to everyone.

705
00:26:52,041 --> 00:26:53,125
Goodbye!

706
00:26:54,041 --> 00:26:55,041
He’s gone!

707
00:26:56,500 --> 00:26:58,500
Thank God he didn’t catch on.

708
00:26:58,791 --> 00:27:00,416
I mean, at first we were really scared…

709
00:27:00,416 --> 00:27:01,250
Ghasem, shut up!

710
00:27:02,125 --> 00:27:04,625
You too please go home,

711
00:27:04,666 --> 00:27:06,166
And rest until tomorrow.

712
00:27:06,250 --> 00:27:06,875
Go ahead.

713
00:27:09,500 --> 00:27:10,125
Get up, let’s go!

714
00:27:10,250 --> 00:27:10,791
Get up!

715
00:27:11,416 --> 00:27:13,500
G… g… go home?

716
00:27:14,500 --> 00:27:16,166
Dustali, where?

717
00:27:16,250 --> 00:27:18,500
I didn’t say a word to Shir-Ali

718
00:27:18,500 --> 00:27:20,166
So I could deal with you myself!

719
00:27:20,250 --> 00:27:21,500
But I’ll leave you alone tonight.

720
00:27:21,500 --> 00:27:23,000
Come on, damn you, go to bed!

721
00:27:23,041 --> 00:27:25,125
I’d rather face Shir-Ali’s cleaver

722
00:27:25,125 --> 00:27:27,750
Than go back to that bed with you!

723
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:28,625
Tonight,

724
00:27:28,666 --> 00:27:30,750
Let Dustali sleep with us,

725
00:27:30,750 --> 00:27:32,166
I’ll talk to him in the morning.

726
00:27:33,250 --> 00:27:34,416
Mama, mama…

727
00:27:34,750 --> 00:27:35,500
Ghamar!

728
00:27:36,500 --> 00:27:37,875
Where are you, Ghamar?

729
00:27:37,875 --> 00:27:40,041
Lock this girl up!

730
00:27:40,125 --> 00:27:41,000
Mama, so

731
00:27:41,000 --> 00:27:43,291
Did you cut off Daddy Dustali’s family jewels?

732
00:27:43,291 --> 00:27:45,250
Oh my! What kind of talk is that? (Ghamar laughs)

733
00:27:45,250 --> 00:27:47,125
What are you doing up there?

734
00:27:47,125 --> 00:27:48,375
Oh, my God!

735
00:27:48,375 --> 00:27:49,625
Don’t fall, girl!

736
00:27:49,625 --> 00:27:51,916
When her mom was chasing me with a knife,

737
00:27:51,916 --> 00:27:53,875
This girl was saying, “Cut it, Mom!” (He speaks with mimicry and mockery)

738
00:27:53,875 --> 00:27:55,875
(Crowd laughter)

739
00:27:55,875 --> 00:27:58,375
Bravo, girl! Bravo!

740
00:27:58,791 --> 00:27:59,916
Tell me,

741
00:28:00,500 --> 00:28:02,416
If your husband misbehaves,

742
00:28:02,500 --> 00:28:04,125
Will you cut it off or not? Huh?

743
00:28:04,666 --> 00:28:07,125
Of course I will! - Get up, let’s go, dear!

744
00:28:07,166 --> 00:28:08,625
Right at the root?

745
00:28:09,416 --> 00:28:10,875
Right at the root!

746
00:28:10,916 --> 00:28:12,500
You son-of-a-bitch!

747
00:28:12,500 --> 00:28:13,500
Have some shame.

748
00:28:13,500 --> 00:28:14,666
Have some decency!

749
00:28:14,666 --> 00:28:15,875
You put words in the child’s mouth,

750
00:28:15,916 --> 00:28:17,541
So tomorrow it reaches her suitors’ ears?

751
00:28:17,541 --> 00:28:18,625
Oh God

752
00:28:18,625 --> 00:28:21,041
Oh God, I wish I had no relatives!

753
00:28:21,125 --> 00:28:23,750
Are you relatives or what!

754
00:28:23,916 --> 00:28:25,791
Moment… Moment

755
00:28:25,875 --> 00:28:26,791
If cutting is bad,

756
00:28:26,875 --> 00:28:27,625
Then why were you

757
00:28:27,666 --> 00:28:29,666
Cutting that poor wretch?

758
00:28:29,750 --> 00:28:30,541
He’s right!

759
00:28:30,625 --> 00:28:31,791
If he’d been any slower,

760
00:28:31,875 --> 00:28:34,541
Dustali-Khan would be a eunuch now!

761
00:28:34,625 --> 00:28:36,875
Reminds you of your ancestors, you old wreck of a Shazdeh!

762
00:28:36,916 --> 00:28:38,041
What business is it of yours anyway!

763
00:28:38,041 --> 00:28:39,666
Since when are you in charge of my husband!

764
00:28:39,666 --> 00:28:41,125
Are you the police chief of this city!

765
00:28:41,166 --> 00:28:42,500
What’s it to me anyway!

766
00:28:42,500 --> 00:28:45,666
To hell with that Dustali and his noble member!

767
00:28:45,666 --> 00:28:46,750
Enough already, Asdollah!

768
00:28:47,041 --> 00:28:49,041
Just one piece of advice!

769
00:28:49,916 --> 00:28:51,166
The kitchen knife is too good for it!

770
00:28:51,166 --> 00:28:53,375
Next time you cut off your husband’s family jewels,

771
00:28:53,375 --> 00:28:55,125
Use this pencil sharpener!

772
00:28:56,625 --> 00:28:57,500
Honestly!

773
00:29:00,750 --> 00:29:03,500
I’m too good to talk to these rascals and thugs.

774
00:29:03,750 --> 00:29:04,541
Get up, Ghamar!

775
00:29:04,625 --> 00:29:05,375
Get up, let’s go.

776
00:29:05,500 --> 00:29:06,791
Get up, let’s go!

777
00:29:09,625 --> 00:29:11,000
Now do you see what I meant?

778
00:29:11,000 --> 00:29:12,041
Oh man…

779
00:29:12,375 --> 00:29:14,250
If you’d thrown your party tonight,

780
00:29:14,416 --> 00:29:16,416
With music, singing and drinking,

781
00:29:16,416 --> 00:29:18,916
These chest-beaters would cut you to pieces!

782
00:29:19,375 --> 00:29:21,125
I’ll give him what he deserves!

783
00:29:21,875 --> 00:29:23,625
He went and brought the neighborhood thugs

784
00:29:23,625 --> 00:29:25,875
To my door! To beat their chests!

785
00:29:26,125 --> 00:29:26,500
He thinks,

786
00:29:26,500 --> 00:29:28,750
I’m afraid of that Seyed and his thugs!

787
00:29:28,791 --> 00:29:30,166
He doesn’t know me yet!

788
00:29:30,625 --> 00:29:33,125
Why are you two at war?

789
00:29:33,375 --> 00:29:34,250
Come on now…

790
00:29:34,291 --> 00:29:36,250
Don’t play backgammon together

791
00:29:36,250 --> 00:29:37,250
If it makes you fight!

792
00:29:37,875 --> 00:29:40,250
After all, he’s getting old.

793
00:29:40,500 --> 00:29:41,666
He’s the head of the family.

794
00:29:41,666 --> 00:29:42,250
Heh! (He sneers)

795
00:29:42,291 --> 00:29:43,916
Tomorrow, just pop over to see him,

796
00:29:43,916 --> 00:29:45,625
And kiss and make up.

797
00:29:45,625 --> 00:29:46,250
Me, go!?

798
00:29:46,625 --> 00:29:48,541
Me, go to his house?

799
00:29:48,625 --> 00:29:50,250
Not that I’m fond of him either!

800
00:29:50,250 --> 00:29:51,916
Go and apologize to him!

801
00:29:52,000 --> 00:29:53,500
Me, apologize! Heh…

802
00:29:54,250 --> 00:29:56,000
I’m begging you, dear.

803
00:29:56,000 --> 00:29:57,791
Forgive him, for my sake.

804
00:29:58,500 --> 00:30:00,041
Let it go!

805
00:30:00,875 --> 00:30:02,625
Poor me, stuck in the middle.

806
00:30:02,625 --> 00:30:04,375
I don’t know what I should do!

807
00:30:04,416 --> 00:30:06,166
Think of me a little too!

808
00:30:06,250 --> 00:30:07,666
You’re my husband,

809
00:30:07,750 --> 00:30:08,875
And he’s my brother!

810
00:30:09,916 --> 00:30:11,416
Pretend I’m your servant girl

811
00:30:11,500 --> 00:30:13,375
And free me as an act of charity!

812
00:30:14,625 --> 00:30:16,125
It’s gotten so bad that my brother

813
00:30:16,125 --> 00:30:17,625
Is cutting me off too!

814
00:30:17,666 --> 00:30:18,750
Tonight he was saying,

815
00:30:18,750 --> 00:30:20,500
Either your husband or your family!

816
00:30:20,875 --> 00:30:22,000
Bravo bravo bravo bravo!

817
00:30:22,041 --> 00:30:23,375
What a noble man!

818
00:30:24,875 --> 00:30:25,375
Bravo!

819
00:30:26,291 --> 00:30:28,166
What a great gentleman!

820
00:30:28,250 --> 00:30:29,291
Bravo!

821
00:30:30,125 --> 00:30:30,666
By the way,

822
00:30:30,750 --> 00:30:32,625
Tell me, which brother of yours said that?

823
00:30:33,250 --> 00:30:35,416
That major who thinks he’s a colonel?

824
00:30:35,500 --> 00:30:36,291
Heh!

825
00:30:37,125 --> 00:30:38,125
Or, the other one!

826
00:30:38,250 --> 00:30:41,000
That hero of the Kazerun war!

827
00:30:41,625 --> 00:30:43,125
Napoleon of the present era!

828
00:30:43,750 --> 00:30:45,250
Iron man!

829
00:30:46,125 --> 00:30:47,166
Man of God!

830
00:30:47,250 --> 00:30:48,791
Yes, he’s a man of God too!

831
00:30:48,916 --> 00:30:51,375
Tonight he held a mourning for Muslim ibn Aqil!

832
00:30:57,375 --> 00:30:58,125
Bravo.

833
00:30:59,041 --> 00:31:00,750
That’s what you call a man of God!

834
00:31:02,166 --> 00:31:04,125
That’s what you call brave and fearless!

835
00:31:04,125 --> 00:31:05,875
He cut off his own nieces’ water!

836
00:31:05,875 --> 00:31:08,041
Just like Shemr did at Karbala!

837
00:31:09,250 --> 00:31:10,750
Who can one even complain to!

838
00:31:16,583 --> 00:31:17,166
By the way!

839
00:31:17,166 --> 00:31:18,916
For lunch tomorrow, make herb rice with fish,

840
00:31:18,916 --> 00:31:21,041
Shir-Ali is coming over for lunch!

841
00:31:22,166 --> 00:31:24,416
I’ve long promised Shir-Ali the butcher

842
00:31:24,458 --> 00:31:25,541
To invite him over

843
00:31:25,583 --> 00:31:27,333
And treat him to herb rice with fish.

844
00:31:31,166 --> 00:31:31,833
Tomorrow morning,

845
00:31:31,916 --> 00:31:33,541
Send Saeid to fetch the Colonel’s servant

846
00:31:33,541 --> 00:31:34,666
To come help you.

847
00:31:34,791 --> 00:31:36,791
♪ Mahur piece – Faramarz Payvar and Hossein Tehrani ♪

848
00:31:49,125 --> 00:31:50,291
Oh man!

849
00:31:50,416 --> 00:31:51,416
Give it here!

850
00:31:51,625 --> 00:31:54,750
How slow you are!

851
00:31:54,750 --> 00:31:56,041
Have you been flirting all morning

852
00:31:56,125 --> 00:31:57,750
Or cleaning fish? Huh?

853
00:31:59,250 --> 00:32:01,125
Fine, feed this damned Shir-Ali

854
00:32:01,166 --> 00:32:02,750
Herb rice with fish if you must,

855
00:32:02,875 --> 00:32:04,125
But I beg you, on your father’s soul,

856
00:32:04,125 --> 00:32:05,541
Don’t say a word about last night!

857
00:32:05,541 --> 00:32:06,750
This man is handy with a knife!

858
00:32:06,750 --> 00:32:07,750
He’s crazy!

859
00:32:08,125 --> 00:32:10,500
If he kills someone, the blood is on your hands!

860
00:32:10,500 --> 00:32:13,125
Everyone does whatever they like to me,

861
00:32:13,166 --> 00:32:15,375
And my own wife takes his side!

862
00:32:16,416 --> 00:32:18,416
Tell me, are you my wife or a spy!

863
00:32:18,416 --> 00:32:20,291
It’s bad enough you told Aziz-Saltaneh

864
00:32:20,375 --> 00:32:22,000
Her husband’s been fooling with Shir-Ali’s wife,

865
00:32:22,041 --> 00:32:22,500
That’s enough!

866
00:32:22,541 --> 00:32:24,625
The scandal Aziz-Saltaneh made

867
00:32:24,625 --> 00:32:26,250
Is enough for seven generations of Dustali-Khans!

868
00:32:26,541 --> 00:32:28,625
I didn’t tell Aziz-Saltaneh anything!

869
00:32:28,625 --> 00:32:30,041
But if I’d known,

870
00:32:30,041 --> 00:32:31,125
I certainly would have!

871
00:32:31,291 --> 00:32:34,625
A shame to hide the virtuous family’s masterpieces!

872
00:32:35,166 --> 00:32:37,166
These are the cream of the nobility!

873
00:32:37,250 --> 00:32:38,250
(He laughs with mockery)

874
00:32:38,250 --> 00:32:40,250
The nobles of this country,

875
00:32:40,250 --> 00:32:42,750
Can’t hold their heads up for shame!

876
00:32:42,750 --> 00:32:45,125
One of their noblest nobles

877
00:32:45,166 --> 00:32:46,875
Has been fooling with a butcher’s wife!

878
00:32:48,125 --> 00:32:48,791
Hopefully they won’t,

879
00:32:48,875 --> 00:32:51,791
For the crime of soiling the nobles’ dignity,

880
00:32:52,916 --> 00:32:54,666
Bump him off!

881
00:32:54,916 --> 00:32:56,125
My dear!

882
00:32:56,125 --> 00:32:57,250
My life!

883
00:32:57,250 --> 00:32:58,666
Have mercy on yourself!

884
00:32:58,750 --> 00:33:01,291
Shir-Ali won’t stand to hear it!

885
00:33:01,375 --> 00:33:02,666
To this crazy man,

886
00:33:02,750 --> 00:33:04,166
If you say a word about his wife,

887
00:33:04,166 --> 00:33:05,125
First of all,

888
00:33:05,125 --> 00:33:07,250
He’ll chop you to pieces with his cleaver!

889
00:33:07,250 --> 00:33:08,750
Who knows

890
00:33:08,750 --> 00:33:10,250
What I’ll tell Shir-Ali!

891
00:33:10,250 --> 00:33:10,875
First of all!

892
00:33:11,250 --> 00:33:12,500
Even if I do tell him,

893
00:33:12,500 --> 00:33:13,625
I know how to say it!

894
00:33:13,666 --> 00:33:14,500
Second!

895
00:33:14,500 --> 00:33:15,666
I’m not a little child

896
00:33:15,666 --> 00:33:16,875
Who doesn’t know what he’s doing!

897
00:33:16,916 --> 00:33:17,500
Third!

898
00:33:17,666 --> 00:33:19,916
I don’t have the patience to explain! Fourth!

899
00:33:19,916 --> 00:33:21,750
Hurry up! It’s already noon!

900
00:33:24,250 --> 00:33:25,625
You’re so slow,

901
00:33:25,666 --> 00:33:27,750
Hurry up, get moving! It’s noon!

902
00:33:29,375 --> 00:33:31,041
Get up and pour a little water on my hands, get up!

903
00:33:31,125 --> 00:33:34,250
♪ Mahur piece – Faramarz Payvar and Hossein Tehrani ♪

904
00:33:34,291 --> 00:33:35,125
What is it, Saeid!

905
00:33:35,541 --> 00:33:36,875
They’ve come from the pharmacy.

906
00:33:38,291 --> 00:33:39,250
Hello Mr. Doctor.

907
00:33:39,250 --> 00:33:39,625
Hello.

908
00:33:40,625 --> 00:33:41,125
What is it?

909
00:33:42,666 --> 00:33:43,416
Has something happened?

910
00:33:43,916 --> 00:33:44,541
What is it?

911
00:33:44,541 --> 00:33:46,250
I don’t know who’s behind this…

912
00:33:46,250 --> 00:33:47,291
Shh… quiet!

913
00:33:49,416 --> 00:33:50,000
Sorry. - What is it?

914
00:33:50,541 --> 00:33:53,125
I don’t know which scoundrel is behind this!

915
00:33:53,250 --> 00:33:54,875
They say, your wife’s brother,

916
00:33:54,875 --> 00:33:56,166
Has spread a rumor in town

917
00:33:56,250 --> 00:33:57,916
That our medicines are un-Islamic!

918
00:33:57,916 --> 00:33:59,666
Either he wants to annoy you,

919
00:33:59,750 --> 00:34:01,250
Or someone put him up to it!

920
00:34:08,000 --> 00:34:09,250
Pay no attention.

921
00:34:09,375 --> 00:34:11,250
Go open the pharmacy right away.

922
00:34:11,250 --> 00:34:12,375
I’m afraid!

923
00:34:12,416 --> 00:34:13,541
Today,

924
00:34:13,916 --> 00:34:15,250
While there’s still time,

925
00:34:15,250 --> 00:34:17,125
You must do something, Doctor!

926
00:34:17,125 --> 00:34:19,500
These rumors come from your wife’s brother!

927
00:34:19,500 --> 00:34:21,375
Have a word with him,

928
00:34:21,416 --> 00:34:22,500
So he can set things right.

929
00:34:24,375 --> 00:34:25,375
Honestly, now

930
00:34:25,375 --> 00:34:27,750
No one sets foot in our pharmacy!

931
00:34:28,375 --> 00:34:30,416
You and I have no other business!

932
00:34:30,916 --> 00:34:34,375
If I find that worthless man is behind this,

933
00:34:35,125 --> 00:34:36,916
I’ll make him pay so dearly that…

934
00:34:37,041 --> 00:34:39,500
They won’t buy our medicine… fine, let them…

935
00:34:39,875 --> 00:34:43,041
But this talk has really spread in the neighborhood!

936
00:34:43,750 --> 00:34:46,291
They’ve accused poor me of not being a Muslim!

937
00:34:46,541 --> 00:34:47,916
Honestly, I don’t dare

938
00:34:48,000 --> 00:34:49,750
Open the pharmacy today, Doctor!

939
00:34:50,125 --> 00:34:50,916
Very good…

940
00:34:51,000 --> 00:34:52,000
If that’s how it is,

941
00:34:52,000 --> 00:34:53,125
Close for today,

942
00:34:53,166 --> 00:34:54,000
So that,

943
00:34:54,041 --> 00:34:55,875
By tomorrow, I’ll get to the bottom of it.

944
00:34:56,500 --> 00:34:57,625
But write something

945
00:34:57,625 --> 00:34:59,041
And stick it on the pharmacy door.

946
00:34:59,125 --> 00:35:00,250
Write what?

947
00:35:00,625 --> 00:35:00,750
Write?

948
00:35:00,750 --> 00:35:02,291
Honestly, I don’t know!

949
00:35:02,375 --> 00:35:05,000
But it must sound impressive.

950
00:35:06,916 --> 00:35:08,250
Um… I say, Doctor…

951
00:35:08,750 --> 00:35:10,750
You tell us something, we’ll write it.

952
00:35:12,125 --> 00:35:12,875
Write,

953
00:35:12,916 --> 00:35:15,000
Due to change of decoration,

954
00:35:15,000 --> 00:35:17,625
The pharmacy is closed until further notice.

955
00:35:17,875 --> 00:35:19,750
I’m afraid if we just close it like this,

956
00:35:19,750 --> 00:35:20,875
He’ll think we’re scared of him

957
00:35:20,916 --> 00:35:22,416
And come up with a new trick!

958
00:35:22,750 --> 00:35:23,791
Not a bad idea.

959
00:35:23,791 --> 00:35:25,500
I’d better get to work right away.

960
00:35:26,000 --> 00:35:28,000
And you tell your wife’s brother

961
00:35:28,000 --> 00:35:29,916
He’d better stop stirring up trouble!

962
00:35:30,375 --> 00:35:33,291
I’ll definitely have a word with my wife’s brother.

963
00:35:33,375 --> 00:35:34,375
Goodbye.

964
00:35:35,041 --> 00:35:36,916
I’ll fix my wife’s brother so badly

965
00:35:36,916 --> 00:35:38,375
That seven brothers of his

966
00:35:38,375 --> 00:35:39,416
Will weep over him!

967
00:35:42,791 --> 00:35:44,750
You people did something to him!

968
00:35:44,750 --> 00:35:46,375
You’ve done away with him!

969
00:35:46,375 --> 00:35:49,000
I’ll make you all pay!

970
00:35:49,041 --> 00:35:51,000
Honestly, what we saw with our own eyes,

971
00:35:51,000 --> 00:35:53,166
We’ll tell you, to put your mind at ease.

972
00:35:53,250 --> 00:35:54,375
This Mr. Dustali-Khan,

973
00:35:54,375 --> 00:35:56,125
Was very scared of you.

974
00:35:56,875 --> 00:35:58,375
Last night after your fight,

975
00:35:58,416 --> 00:35:59,625
When you went home,

976
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:01,166
In that same room

977
00:36:01,250 --> 00:36:03,125
You just saw with your own eyes,

978
00:36:03,166 --> 00:36:04,041
We made up a bed for him.

979
00:36:05,000 --> 00:36:06,125
He went to sleep.

980
00:36:06,750 --> 00:36:08,416
In the morning when we took him tea,

981
00:36:08,416 --> 00:36:09,750
We saw his bed was there,

982
00:36:10,125 --> 00:36:11,791
But Mr. Dustali-Khan himself was gone!

983
00:36:12,291 --> 00:36:14,916
He wasn’t one to go off without a word!

984
00:36:14,916 --> 00:36:16,500
How am I supposed to believe you!

985
00:36:16,500 --> 00:36:18,041
Maybe you killed him!

986
00:36:18,125 --> 00:36:19,666
Maybe in a fight over property,

987
00:36:19,750 --> 00:36:21,250
You threw his body down the well!

988
00:36:21,250 --> 00:36:22,375
You know where he is!

989
00:36:22,375 --> 00:36:23,125
Tell me where he is!

990
00:36:23,166 --> 00:36:24,250
Tell me, you liar!

991
00:36:24,291 --> 00:36:26,125
Honestly, Sir has hired a car,

992
00:36:26,166 --> 00:36:28,916
They’re searching for him everywhere.

993
00:36:28,916 --> 00:36:30,375
Yeah, sure!

994
00:36:30,375 --> 00:36:32,666
Your master’s hiding out of fear of me!

995
00:36:32,666 --> 00:36:33,666
To your master say,

996
00:36:33,750 --> 00:36:35,541
You kept my husband here by force last night!

997
00:36:35,541 --> 00:36:37,000
Wherever you hid him,

998
00:36:37,000 --> 00:36:38,416
Bring him back to me this very day!

999
00:36:38,625 --> 00:36:40,625
Or I’ll file a complaint with the police!

1000
00:36:42,625 --> 00:36:44,250
I’ll go to the Detective Bureau!

1001
00:36:45,416 --> 00:36:47,916
I’ll stop the Minister of Justice’s car in the street!

1002
00:36:50,916 --> 00:36:53,416
(She starts crying)

1003
00:36:58,125 --> 00:36:59,125
Aziz Khanom!

1004
00:36:59,875 --> 00:37:00,750
Aziz Khanom!

1005
00:37:01,750 --> 00:37:03,125
What’s the matter, Lady Aziz-Saltaneh?

1006
00:37:03,166 --> 00:37:04,791
Oh my husband! - What is it?

1007
00:37:05,250 --> 00:37:06,041
What is it, my dear?

1008
00:37:06,625 --> 00:37:07,250
Something happened?

1009
00:37:07,250 --> 00:37:10,000
My poor husband has been missing since last night!

1010
00:37:10,125 --> 00:37:11,166
Missing?

1011
00:37:11,250 --> 00:37:12,291
Dustali-Khan?

1012
00:37:12,625 --> 00:37:14,625
How does a grown man go missing?

1013
00:37:15,375 --> 00:37:16,000
I know,

1014
00:37:16,000 --> 00:37:17,625
They’ve hidden him somewhere!

1015
00:37:17,625 --> 00:37:18,250
I know!

1016
00:37:18,250 --> 00:37:19,500
Don’t worry!

1017
00:37:19,666 --> 00:37:21,041
Poor innocent Dustali-Khan!

1018
00:37:21,125 --> 00:37:22,250
Now come in, have some tea.

1019
00:37:22,250 --> 00:37:22,791
Come in.

1020
00:37:22,791 --> 00:37:24,875
No, I must hurry before they do something to him,

1021
00:37:24,916 --> 00:37:26,500
Maybe I can find him. - Well, it’s not that easy,

1022
00:37:26,500 --> 00:37:27,416
- You can’t find him!

1023
00:37:27,416 --> 00:37:28,666
But don’t worry! - Then what should I do?

1024
00:37:29,291 --> 00:37:31,625
Out of my devotion to you,

1025
00:37:31,666 --> 00:37:33,500
And to Dustali-Khan as well,

1026
00:37:33,541 --> 00:37:35,666
I’ll help you find him sooner.

1027
00:37:36,166 --> 00:37:36,750
Lady,

1028
00:37:36,750 --> 00:37:38,625
I know these nasty relatives of ours

1029
00:37:38,625 --> 00:37:39,916
Better than you do.

1030
00:37:40,375 --> 00:37:41,791
Isn’t this fish cleaned yet?

1031
00:37:42,500 --> 00:37:44,250
From the start of your marriage,

1032
00:37:44,250 --> 00:37:46,875
They couldn’t bear to see you and Dustali-Khan happy!

1033
00:37:50,375 --> 00:37:52,375
Come in, please, come in.

1034
00:37:53,083 --> 00:37:55,125
They want that tramp of a relative of theirs,

1035
00:37:55,208 --> 00:37:56,083
That widow,

1036
00:37:56,083 --> 00:37:57,000
Farrokh Lagha,

1037
00:37:57,000 --> 00:37:58,333
To be foisted on Dustali-Khan again!

1038
00:37:58,333 --> 00:37:58,958
They can dream it!

1039
00:37:58,958 --> 00:37:59,708
Well before you,

1040
00:37:59,708 --> 00:38:01,375
She was supposed to become Dustali’s wife!

1041
00:38:01,375 --> 00:38:02,333
Shameless ones!

1042
00:38:02,458 --> 00:38:03,833
This precious Farrokh Lagha of theirs

1043
00:38:03,833 --> 00:38:05,333
Should go marry the Angel of Death!

1044
00:38:05,333 --> 00:38:07,208
I’ll make them pay!

1045
00:38:28,125 --> 00:38:30,000
I know that the police chief

1046
00:38:30,041 --> 00:38:32,000
Was a friend of your late father!

1047
00:38:32,041 --> 00:38:32,625
Oh?

1048
00:38:32,666 --> 00:38:34,000
If he doesn’t recognize you, don’t be shy.

1049
00:38:34,041 --> 00:38:34,791
Introduce yourself.

1050
00:38:35,875 --> 00:38:37,291
Lady Aziz-Saltaneh!

1051
00:38:37,291 --> 00:38:38,666
If you ask me,

1052
00:38:38,666 --> 00:38:39,166
Tell him

1053
00:38:39,166 --> 00:38:41,125
You doubt your husband is even alive!

1054
00:38:41,125 --> 00:38:42,500
(She cries)

1055
00:38:42,500 --> 00:38:44,166
Unless force is used,

1056
00:38:44,250 --> 00:38:45,625
They’ll never tell

1057
00:38:45,625 --> 00:38:47,875
Where they’ve hidden poor Dustali!

1058
00:38:47,916 --> 00:38:48,916
Impossible!

1059
00:38:50,041 --> 00:38:51,166
Sir and Dustali,

1060
00:38:51,250 --> 00:38:52,750
Have been feuding for years

1061
00:38:52,750 --> 00:38:54,000
Over a piece of property!

1062
00:38:54,000 --> 00:38:55,000
You remember?

1063
00:38:55,166 --> 00:38:56,625
Well then, what are you waiting for!

1064
00:38:57,375 --> 00:38:58,541
Even better!

1065
00:38:58,875 --> 00:39:00,666
Just say they killed Dustali-Khan!

1066
00:39:01,041 --> 00:39:04,125
Say they buried his body under that rose arbor!

1067
00:39:04,125 --> 00:39:05,375
Why under the roses?

1068
00:39:05,875 --> 00:39:07,375
This Mr. Napoleon,

1069
00:39:07,500 --> 00:39:10,625
Would give his life for his beautiful roses!

1070
00:39:11,000 --> 00:39:11,791
Heartless man,

1071
00:39:11,791 --> 00:39:12,791
Loves a rosebush

1072
00:39:12,875 --> 00:39:14,416
More than his own child!

1073
00:39:15,125 --> 00:39:16,666
And you expect him, over property,

1074
00:39:16,750 --> 00:39:18,041
To show your husband mercy?

1075
00:39:18,541 --> 00:39:20,750
When the police, looking for Dustali’s body,

1076
00:39:20,750 --> 00:39:23,125
Come dig up the roses,

1077
00:39:23,125 --> 00:39:25,000
Mr. Napoleon,

1078
00:39:25,000 --> 00:39:25,750
Will talk!

1079
00:39:25,791 --> 00:39:26,750
He’ll tell them

1080
00:39:26,791 --> 00:39:28,916
Where they’ve hidden poor Dustali-Khan!

1081
00:39:29,000 --> 00:39:31,125
I’m afraid they won’t believe me!

1082
00:39:31,125 --> 00:39:31,625
Why?

1083
00:39:32,375 --> 00:39:34,416
But the ground under the roses is flat!

1084
00:39:34,500 --> 00:39:35,375
It’s all lawn!

1085
00:39:35,625 --> 00:39:36,791
For burying a person,

1086
00:39:36,875 --> 00:39:38,250
Of Dustali’s size,

1087
00:39:38,500 --> 00:39:40,875
You’d need to dig a grave, wouldn’t you!?

1088
00:39:42,500 --> 00:39:44,041
Don’t you… worry about that.

1089
00:39:44,125 --> 00:39:44,791
Leave that to me!

1090
00:39:45,250 --> 00:39:47,500
Just don’t waste any time.

1091
00:39:47,875 --> 00:39:49,916
The more time you lose,

1092
00:39:49,916 --> 00:39:51,500
The more chance you give them

1093
00:39:51,541 --> 00:39:53,625
To fill Dustali-Khan’s ears and…

1094
00:39:53,625 --> 00:39:54,875
Play with your life

